EXTENSION "ARMDef_The_Contested_Isle_Connacht_BallackOfTytalus" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Contested Isle - Ballack of Tytalus"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ARMDef_The_Contested_Isle_Core_Ext"

    # Ballack of Tytalus (Chapter Five: The Province of Connacht, p47): one character, its stat lines verbatim fields.

    #t55a7f0e66e42cd2ed7d7d5 ^"Ballack of Tytalus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#td108e5b25b535ed37699ad ^"The Covenant of Praesis"]
            ^"Age" STRING "80 (Apparent Age: 65)"
            ^"Personality Trait" STRING "Confident +3, Driven +2, Patient +1"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Contested Isle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 47
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Ballack, the new Lord of Praesis, rejoiced in turning Hibernia’s traditions on the Irish and taking his revenge against Meadhbh. But it speaks to the character of the man that Holzner’s head still hangs from the palisade walls exactly where Meadhbh put it years ago.\n\nHe displays a festering contempt for the Irish magi and their outdated ways and is busy making overtures of support and friendship to both established English covenants and newly-arrived adventurers.\n\nBallack has spent the last year consolidating his hold on the crumbling ruins of Praesis but his war against Meadhbh cost him dearly, and he owes vis and favors to a number of magi. For all his confident swagger he knows that until his debts are repaid his position is merely on loan.\n\nWith his personal resources exhausted, he has been forced to borrow yet more vis and casting tablets from his distant benefactors. He is keen to find a way for the covenant to pay for itself and soon. He cannot be seen to abandon his prize."
    }

}
